{"text": "D. Bruce Hoffman\n\nPRACTICES\nAntitrust and Competition\n\u201cAntitust Ligation\n(Consumer Protection and\n\u2018Advertsing Review\nCriminal Antivust Defense and\nInvestigations\nCustors and Intemational Trade\nMerger Review\nReta\nEnergy Sector Security Team\n\u2018Consumer Products\n\nCONTACT\n\u2018bhofiman@hunton.com\nWashington, DC\n202955 1619\n202782201\n\nEDUCATION\nJD, Unversity of Florida, high\nhonors, W.D. MeDonald Prize\n(fest in class), Order ofthe Cort,\nBoard Member, Florida Law\nReview, 1992\nBA, Penn Stato Unversity, high\ndistinction, 1988\n\nBAR ADMISSIONS\nDistrict of Columbia\nFlorida\n\nHunton & Willams LLP\n\nBruce's practice focuses on antitrust and unfair competition,\nincluding investigations and litigation.\n\nBruce serves as head of the global competition practice at Hunton & Williams,\n\u2018where he focuses on antitrust and unfair competition, including merger reviews,\ngovernment investigations, and private and government antitrust litigation. Bruce\nalso represents a broad range of cients in general commercial tigation,\n\nBefore joining the firm, Bruce served at the Federal Trade Commission in\n\u2018Washington, DC, as Deputy Director and previously Associate Director of\nRegional Litigation ofthe Bureau of Competition. During his tenure at the FTC,\nhhe oversaw the Bureau's competition programs, activities and investigations and\ned numerous high-profile cases involving mergers, price fixing,\n\u2018monopolizations, conspiracies and other issues in a broad range of industries.\nHe has also participated in amicus brief efforts before the US Supreme Court\nBruce is admitted to practice before the US Supreme Court, the US Courts of\n\u2018Appeals for the DC, Sixth, Eighth and Eleventh Circuits; the US District Courts,\nfor the District of Columbia, the District of Colorado, the Southern, Middle and\n\u2018Northem Districts of Florida, and the Western District of Wisconsin; and in the\nDistrict of Columbia and all state courts in Florida,\n\n\u2018Throughout his career, Bruce has been recognized as a highly respectod\nlecturer and author on numerous topics. He regularly speaks a legal and\nindustry seminars and conferences across the country, and publishes articles in\na broad range of journals, magazines and other publications\n\nRelevant Experience\n\n+ Represented one of the worlds largest supermarket chains before the Federal\n\u2018Trade Commission in connection with strategic divestitures of grocery assets\nin the United States.\n+ Represented a leading provider of funeral, cremation and cemetery services\nbefore the Federal Trade Commission in investigation into proposed\nacquisition of another provider of funeral, cremation and cemetery services.\n+ Represented Universal Music Group before the Federal Trade Commission in\nits $1.9 bition acquisition ofthe recorded music business of EMI Music. After a\n\u2018Second Request and an extensive investigation, the FTC voted \u00a7-0 to close its\ninvestigation without requiring divestitures or other remedies.\n\n+ Represented Delta Air Lines in the antitrust review of a proposed La Guardia",
